<title>USA: Raytheon says beat Q1 EPS estimate by $0.05.</title>
<headline>Raytheon says beat Q1 EPS estimate by $0.05.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co's first quarter earlings of $0.78 a share beat Wall Street estimates by $0.05, company spokesman Robert McWade said Monday.</p>
<p>In a statement announcing the results, which included operating income up 15.4 percent to $339.5 million, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Dennis Picard said, &quot;We are pleased to report that Raytheon had strong operating income in the first quarter, particularly in the Electronics segment.&quot;</p>
</text>
